session Dual_Write_Schedule_Validator = Dual_Write_Core +
  description "
    The certified schedule-validator companion for the Dual-Write core: it
    closes the landed point decider's totality gap (external review finding
    F2). The landed executor state_of_labels evaluates blind label folds, so
    schedule_bad_crash_at returns verdicts on label lists that form no
    dw_exec_trace at all; its correctness theorems quantify over valid traces
    only. This session adds a total step function proved equivalent to
    dw_exec_step, its Kleisli fold proved equivalent to dw_exec_trace, and a
    three-valued verdict (Invalid / Safe / Bad) that rejects exactly the
    trace-less schedules and agrees with the landed decider on valid ones,
    completing the schedule-level story the effect-tier decider delegates to
    the store tier (gate ruling D-S5-2). Everything is code-exported to
    Standard ML and the worked examples are kernel-evaluated (code_simp).
    Additive companion session: the AFP-locked core is imported unchanged,
    byte-untouched. Sorry-free and axiom-free over the imported base.
  "
  options [timeout = 600]
  theories
    Dual_Write_Schedule_Validator
